# Drafted by Gemini (R24 mayor), edited.

~ mob_start
if days_since.ct_clock >= 4
-> mob_late
endif
Narrator: Torch smoke and wet wool thicken the porch air while a mill hand loops fresh hemp around his fist.
ct_mob_leader [angry]: Stand aside, strangers. Somerton put his seal to every permit those hare-masked devils asked for, and the Oak is thirsty tonight.
wendel_somerton [afraid]: Through the bolted shutters, you hear me! That was municipal routine, pure paperwork, I never signed for a burning!
* [Persuasion DC 15] Talk the crowd down -> mob_saved_talk | mob_angry
* [Intimidation DC 15] Face them down -> mob_saved_scare | mob_angry
* [if item:ledger_of_debts] Hand over Alda's ledger of debts -> mob_ledger
* Take Wendel into our custody -> mob_custody
* [ends:save_the_mayor] Let the crowd have him -> mob_jail
* Not now -> END

~ mob_angry
Narrator: A low growl ripples from the back row, and boots scrape closer across the gravel.
ct_mob_leader [angry]: Fine talk does not raise the dead, friend. Give us the doorway or get out of our road.
set ct_mob_angry
quest save_the_mayor mob
-> mob_menu

~ mob_menu
ct_mob_leader [angry]: Well? Either you have business with the man inside or we do.
* [if item:ledger_of_debts] Hand over Alda's ledger of debts -> mob_ledger
* Take Wendel into our custody -> mob_custody
* [ends:save_the_mayor] Let the crowd have him -> mob_jail
* Not now -> END

~ mob_saved_talk
Narrator: One by one, the pitchforks dip toward the mud as the mill hand rubs his jaw and looks to his neighbours.
ct_mob_leader [weary]: A fool is not a cultist, I grant you that much. Come on, lads, there is ash enough to clear before we make more.
set ct_mayor_settled
set ct_mayor_fate = "saved"
quest save_the_mayor saved
-> mob_end

~ mob_saved_scare
Narrator: The mill hand looks from the soot of the moor on your sleeves to the rope in his palm, and lets the coil drop.
ct_mob_leader [afraid]: Nobody here is looking to cross blades with the lot of you. Keep the old windbag, then, and welcome to him.
set ct_mayor_settled
set ct_mayor_fate = "saved"
quest save_the_mayor saved
-> mob_end

~ mob_ledger
Narrator: The mill hand holds the oilskin pages to a lantern, his thumb tracing the inked names and tallies in silence.
ct_mob_leader [angry]: Here are the real ones who bought and sold us, writ in their own clerk's hand. Leave Somerton, lads, we have proper doors to knock on.
take ledger_of_debts
set ct_mayor_settled
set ct_mayor_fate = "saved"
quest save_the_mayor saved
-> mob_end

~ mob_custody
Narrator: Iron keys clink as Wendel is marched out between your shoulders toward the constable's lockup, his collar pulled high.
ct_mob_leader [neutral]: Long as he sits behind Doris Squire's bars till the reckoning is done, we can live with that.
doris_squire [neutral]: In you go, Mayor. Straw is dry enough.
set ct_mayor_settled
set ct_mayor_fate = "saved"
quest save_the_mayor saved
-> mob_end

~ mob_jail
Narrator: The shutters splinter inward, and a dozen rough hands haul the mayor out by his velvet lapels toward the lockup.
wendel_somerton [afraid]: Mind the chain of office, I beg you! This is highly irregular!
ct_mob_leader [angry]: Doris can keep him under lock and key till we sort the rope from the law.
set ct_mayor_settled
set ct_mayor_fate = "jailed"
quest save_the_mayor jailed
-> END

~ mob_late
Narrator: The mayor's porch stands empty with its door off the hinges, and across the Round the old oak bears a fresh, pinched face in its bark.
doris_squire [weary]: Came too late for him. Crowd took him at the third bell, and the tree had the rest.
set ct_mayor_settled
set ct_mayor_fate = "lynched"
quest save_the_mayor lynched
-> END

~ mob_end
wendel_somerton [smile]: A delicate civic moment, my friends, and I am glad my calm bearing gave you the opening you needed! Still, Wickermoor does not forget who stood by its chair.
-> END
